  "module": "scene",
  "note": "The globe is cobe (MIT, 12.9 KB, vendored at assets/vendor/cobe.module.js), and the reason it is safe to use is measured rather than assumed: its published build contains zero requestAnimationFrame, zero performance.now and zero Date.now. It owns no clock, so `phi = f(t)` is the entire integration and determinism is a property of the shape rather than a contract someone has to remember. Magic UI's globe is a React wrapper around this same library; we use the library, not the wrapper, so no React enters the engine and its rAF spring loop, which is exactly the thing we must not have, is simply not part of it. The three.js globe in core/three-fx.js stays for the one thing cobe cannot do, a terminator computed as a real hemisphere from a sun vector. This one is prettier and is a tenth of the code.",
